## Claim 5 — Corrected

> The italic type was first used in the Virgil.

**Correction:** Griffo's Aldine italic debuted in the prefatory matter of the Epistole devotissime de Sancta Catharina de Siena, Venice: Aldus Manutius, 19 September 1500. The Virgil of April 1501 was the first book whose main text was printed in italic—not the type's first use.

