## Claim 12 — Corrected

> The Hypnerotomachia Poliphili has never been translated into English.

**Correction:** English translations do exist: Dallington's 1592 partial translation and Godwin's 1999 full translation. The Hypnerotomachia Poliphili has appeared in English as The Dream of Poliphilus / The Dream of Poliphilo. Registry lists English-titled editions in 1888 and 1889 and English-language peer-reviewed treatments in 1951, so 'never been translated into English' is false. The Hypnerotomachia Poliphili has been translated into English: in full by Joscelyn Godwin as Hypnerotomachia Poliphili: The Strife of Love in a Dream (Thames & Hudson, 1999, reissued 2005), and in part in Elizabethan English as Hypnerotomachia. The strife of love in a dreame (London, 1592, signed R.D., attributed to Robert Dallington). The Hypnerotomachia Poliphili has been translated into English: partially by Robert Dallington in 1592 as The Strife of Love in a Dreame, and completely by Joscelyn Godwin in 1999 as Hypnerotomachia Poliphili: The Strife of Love in a Dream (Thames &#x26; Hudson).

